{"ukmt-tmc-2024-regional-crossnumber-01":[{"title":"Solution","body":"Work from the clues that stand alone.\n\n- 5A: $5!=120$. 10D: $4!=24$. 20D: $4\\times8.5=34$. 7A is a two-digit Fibonacci number starting with the 3 of the prime 4D $=23$ (and 20D $=34$ ends in 4), so 7A $=34$.\n- Powers: 3A $=512$ ($8^3$), 8D $=4096$ ($8^4$), 28A $=3125$ ($5^5$), 12D $=625$ ($5^4$).\n- 17A $=\\sqrt{625}=25$; 3D $=50$; 13A $=24+5=29$; 14D $=3125+100=3225$.\n- 15A: $4096\\bmod200=96$. 24D: $1+\\sqrt{4096}=65$. 23A: $50+6=56$. 25A: $4096-3125=971$; 2D: $971\\bmod50=21$.\n- 27A: $(25-2)^2=529$. 25D: $x^2+2x=99$ with $x=9$.\n- 16A: an isosceles triangle with a $76^\\circ$ angle has other angles $76,28$ or $52,52$: the two-digit answer $28$. 19D: with $31.5^\\circ$: angles $31.5,31.5,117$ (the other option $31.5,74.25,74.25$ is not a whole number), so $117$.\n- 21A is a multiple of $111$; it is $444$ (1D is half of it, $222$, and must fit 1A's first digit 2). Then 9A $=222$ and 6D $=444-222=222$.\n- 11D$=22$D$+$square and 11A$=22$D$+1$: with 22D$=425$, 11A$=426$, 11D$=425+36=461$.\n- 1A: $461+\\frac14(21\\times444)=461+2331=2792$. 4D $=23$, 26D $=13$, 18A $=115$.\n\nCompleted answers: Across: 1: 2792, 3: 512, 5: 120, 7: 34, 9: 222, 11: 426, 13: 29, 15: 96, 16: 28, 17: 25, 18: 115, 21: 444, 23: 56, 25: 971, 27: 529, 28: 3125. Down: 1: 222, 2: 21, 3: 50, 4: 23, 6: 222, 8: 4096, 10: 24, 11: 461, 12: 625, 14: 3225, 19: 117, 20: 34, 22: 425, 24: 65, 25: 99, 26: 13.\n\n**Answer: the completed grid above.**"}]}